                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea0c8f64-4b5b-3236-a445-2e8578f21039",
                        "entry_id": "07caa71f-9224-3242-9fb0-f4f2e32271a1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to a garbage dump; rubbishy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd991315-ec3b-4ed0-8a31-aa98583536e5",
                                "sense_id": "ea0c8f64-4b5b-3236-a445-2e8578f21039",
                                "text": "\"I knew it!\" Barry screeched. \"A dump bike for the dummy. Hey, dumpy boy. Dumper! Ha, haaaaaaaaagh!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "979d8865-1d4e-411f-b11a-2fe822c073b2",
                                "sense_id": "ea0c8f64-4b5b-3236-a445-2e8578f21039",
                                "text": "At first, I had no idea you had money, and you didn't seem like a snoot. The place where you were renting was a dumpy place. When you turned out to have money, I was surprised."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6af176d7-fd2a-419d-b486-70edc98d69fb",
                                "sense_id": "ea0c8f64-4b5b-3236-a445-2e8578f21039",
                                "text": "On the other side of the walls was a dumpy, trash-ridden street of the IZ, not far from an old government building of Saddam Hussein."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "83fa6fcf-b623-36f1-a8e5-91991f9d5532",
                "word": "dumpy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2720db6c-66af-416f-9985-5726f1c4fa6d",
                        "entry_id": "83fa6fcf-b623-36f1-a8e5-91991f9d5532",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dumpies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34f7d3b5-5913-370e-8246-7d4d37315609",
                        "entry_id": "83fa6fcf-b623-36f1-a8e5-91991f9d5532",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A short, stout person or animal, especially one of a breed of very short-legged chickens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "060cebe4-1515-4bd8-8c65-4c9e079dfac2",
                                "sense_id": "34f7d3b5-5913-370e-8246-7d4d37315609",
                                "text": "Yet I don't like dumpies either, and Brown says she is little and stout—the better fitted for a wiry, starved-looking chap like you."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8beb779b-2ea4-3aa5-b15a-2b9d47741e87",
                        "entry_id": "83fa6fcf-b623-36f1-a8e5-91991f9d5532",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small bottle of beer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "South-Africa"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf249a7d-5c2c-4bb4-9a16-0ff81193e50d",
                                "sense_id": "8beb779b-2ea4-3aa5-b15a-2b9d47741e87",
                                "text": "Lager-style beer comes in cans or dumpies (small bottles) for around US$1.10."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be3fbebd-93ab-4b61-8a75-7f641a4cb69c",
                                "sense_id": "8beb779b-2ea4-3aa5-b15a-2b9d47741e87",
                                "text": "“Once you start drinking you have many friends drinking with you,” the University of Johannesburg student explained. “I drink whiskey and I drink beer. I drink heavily on weekends but during the week I have about three or four dumpies. I don’t pass out. I just get drunk,” he said."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53da3ab2-6acb-316e-84e1-ce2ab1db609c",
                        "entry_id": "83fa6fcf-b623-36f1-a8e5-91991f9d5532",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of dumpy level."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "ellipsis"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7b37428-ff28-448d-a904-a360bcd25249",
                                "sense_id": "53da3ab2-6acb-316e-84e1-ce2ab1db609c",
                                "text": "Most manufacturers have ceased making dumpies, and a number have even stopped making tilting levels, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
